A||N||6||dwilsonfl||Fuel Tank Lines Help||||5||
Z||000000||dwilsonfl||10-15-2001||12:34 AM||||After replacing the pump last Monday, I got no pressure in the line even though it sounded as if the pump were running. So I need to verify I routed the lines correctly, and/or rewire the splices on the pump. <P>Can someone give me an idea of the three small lines coming from the tank and where they go so I can trace their routes? <P>TIA,<P>David Wilson - 84 SE||||reg||5
Z||000001||Dan87GT||10-15-2001||07:20 AM||||The small line towards the driver side connects to a metal line that goes to the fuel vapor canister(below the drivers side deck grill) the other to lines are the main and return fuel lines that go to the fuel rail(the smaller line is the return line). You should be able to identify all of them according to there size(smallest-vapor canister, med-return line, large-main fuel line). ||||reg||1
Z||000002||tgowens||10-15-2001||08:31 AM||||Make sure that when you installed the new pump that you removed the caps over the inlets that go into the hoses...... it's easy to overlook and that could be the cause of no pressure on the fuel rail. (not trying to insult your intelligence but it has happened to me and I work on these things every day!!)||||reg||1
Z||000003||dwilsonfl||10-16-2001||12:44 AM||||Was able to get up under briefly today, tank was leaking from top. Rivulet of gas running from top to front strap and dripping. It appeared just looking that the hoses were put on correctly. Maybe the pump is wired backwards and pressurizing the tank? More later as this progresses. ||||reg||1
Z||000004||isthiswhereiputausername?||10-16-2001||02:43 PM||||if your tank is leaking.. you can patch it with a putty type of sealer called "steely"  It can be put on with the tank wet and hardens so hard in 15 minutes it can be drilled/tapped.. It is similar to jbweld, but I find this better for gastanks.. I recently fixed mine..it had a few pinholes by the straps..<P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||dwilsonfl||10-16-2001||10:12 PM||||I don't remember any caps on the pump at all. What I do remember is two black lines I had to splice into, and the instructions saying go black to black and gray to the other color.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> So I had a 50-50 chance. GM instructions were wonderful - NOT. I'll get back under Thursday - weather permitting.||||reg||8
Z||000006||HummelHund||10-31-2001||12:48 AM||||It has a pinhole leak under one of the straps. This "steely", can it be found at Autozone?||||reg||1
